WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.092
EXPLAIN shows how PostgreSQL plans to execute the statement.

00:00:04.092 --> 00:00:07.637
The purpose here is not to memorize every plan node.

00:00:07.637 --> 00:00:13.087
It is to build the habit of checking instead of guessing.

00:00:13.087 --> 00:00:19.037
On real workloads, data volume, indexes, statistics, and PostgreSQL version all affect the plan.

00:00:19.037 --> 00:00:25.817
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:33.347
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a new

00:00:33.347 --> 00:00:39.920
block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
